# Whitelist, not blacklist: this repo root holds ~40 agent dot-directories, two
# bfg jars, build/server logs and a real CV pdf. A blacklist would have to name
# every one of them and would silently ship the next thing added. Everything is
# excluded, then only what `next build` reads is let back in.
#
# The load-bearing exclusion is `.env*`: Next inlines `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` at build
# time, so a build that reads the host's `.env.local` bakes live credentials
# into an image layer that survives in the build cache. The two values the
# client bundle genuinely needs come in as build ARGs from docker/.env instead.
*

!package.json
!package-lock.json
!next.config.ts
!next-env.d.ts
!tsconfig.json
!eslint.config.mjs
!AGENTS.md
!src
!public
!scripts
!docker/app/Dockerfile
